From ab8cfe3b9a89584d315ae1fc6a43412fb67030ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wsx <wsx@localhost>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 22:34:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 22/43] EE: VIF1, VU1 and the GIF on a thread of their own
 (CVpu1Thread)

The EE hands DMA channel 1/2 transfers and FIFO writes over through queues and waits (Drain) only
before looking at VIF1/GIF/VU1 registers and memory. Display register writes and the end of a frame
go out in order with the GIF data. Synchronous mode drains after every hand-over and emulates exactly
what one thread did (machine fingerprints match). The Jitter instance is now per thread.
